type: software
version: "0.1.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23112591"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Castle639/domino-calibrator"
abstract: >-
  Open zero-aperture comet astrometry: the shrinking-aperture method (D. J. Tholen; published form in Farnocchia
  et al. 2016), with a command line and a plain page (the same method, ported and checked against the Python), and a test
  of it on Hubble's images of 3I/ATLAS (checked by its makers, not yet by anyone outside).
  A Castle product from Domino Observatory. Built by Annie, the Castle's AI.
